{"step_index":2162,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-16T07:45:51Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-16T13:15:51+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-10-16T13:15:52+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/k4ran/.gemini/antigravity/brain/e2c1cf9f-2dff-4bf4-a974-ef410441acfa/walkthrough.md`\nTotal Lines: 141\nTotal Bytes: 4466\nShowing lines 1 to 141\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: # SmartAGENT v0.2.0 — Agentic Build Walkthrough\n2: \n3: ## What Changed\n4: \n5: Transformed SmartAGENT from a **static regex scanner with optional AI verification** into a **fully autonomous agentic security AI** with a ReAct reasoning loop.\n6: \n7: ### Before (v0.1.0)\n8: ```\n9: smartagent scan . → regex patterns → findings list → (optional) AI verify each\n10: ```\n11: \n12: ### After (v0.2.0)\n13: ```\n14: smartagent chat → interactive agent that thinks, plans, uses tools, and acts autonomously\n15: smartagent agent \"scan for SQL injection\" → one-shot autonomous task\n16: smartagent scan . → still works (unchanged)\n17: ```\n18: \n19: ---\n20: \n21: ## New Files (5)\n22: \n23: ### 1. `smartagent/agent/__init__.py`\n24: Package init exposing `SmartAgent` class.\n25: \n26: ### 2. `smartagent/agent/prompts.py`\n27: ReAct system prompt that teaches the model to:\n28: - Think step-by-step before acting\n29: - Use tools with `Action: tool_name` / `Action Input: args` format\n30: - Return `Final Answer:` when reasoning is complete\n31: - Lists all 8 available tools with descriptions\n32: \n33: ### 3. `smartagent/agent/memory.py`\n34: Sliding-window conversation memory:\n35: - Preserves system prompt (always first message)\n36: - Keeps last 20 messages (configurable)\n37: - Tracks which files have been scanned\n38: - Accumulates findings across tool calls\n39: \n40: ### 4. `smartagent/agent/tools.py`\n41: 8 security-focused tools:\n42: \n43: | Tool | Description |\n44: |---|---|\n45: | `list_files` | Lists code files in a directory, respects ignore patterns |\n46: | `read_file` | Reads file contents with optional line range (`:10-50`) |\n47: | `search_code` | Regex search across all code files (capped at 50 results) |\n48: | `scan_code` | Runs all 4 existing static scanners on a file |\n49: | `get_cwe_info` | Looks up CWE details from embedded 12-entry knowledge base |\n50: | `write_report` | Writes findings to JSON or Markdown report file |\n51: | `run_command` | Sandboxed shell execution (allowlist: git, python, grep, etc.) |\n52: | `fix_code` | Generates remediation template for a CWE + code snippet |\n53: \n54: Also includes an embedded CWE knowledge base (12 entries covering the most common web/code vulns) so the agent can look up vulnerability details without network access.\n55: \n56: ### 5. `smartagent/agent/core.py`\n57: The **ReAct agent loop** — the brain:\n58: - Parses LLM output with regex for `Thought:`, `Action:`, `Action Input:`, `Final Answer:`\n59: - Dispatches tool calls to the `ToolRegistry`\n60: - Injects `Observation:` back into the conversation\n61: - Handles malformed outputs gracefully (nudges the model to retry)\n62: - Enforces 15-iteration safety limit\n63: - Lazy-loads the model (fast startup if model not needed)\n64: - Rich terminal output: colored panels for Thought/Action/Observation/Answer\n65: \n66: ---\n67: \n68: ## Modified Files (4)\n69: \n70: ### `smartagent/ai/model.py`\n71: - Fixed `Tuple[Any, Any]` type hint (was missing `Any` import)\n72: - Added `generate_stream()` method for real-time token streaming via `TextIteratorStreamer`\n73: - Added `Generator` import\n74: \n75: ### `smartagent/config.py`\n76: Added 4 agent config fields:\n77: - `max_agent_iterations: int = 15`\n78: - `agent_temperature: float = 0.3`\n79: - `memory_window: int = 20`\n80: - `allowed_commands: list` (sandboxed shell allowlist)\n81: - Fixed default model ID to `k4ran909/Fluxnat-Coder-3B`\n82: \n83: ### `smartagent/cli.py`\n84: Added 2 new CLI commands:\n85: - **`smartagent chat`** — Interactive REPL with Rich formatting. Supports `exit`, `quit`, `reset`.\n86: - **`smartagent agent \"task\"`** — One-shot autonomous task execution\n87: - Updated version display to `0.2.0 (Agentic)`\n88: - Shows \"Agent Mode: Available\" in system info\n89: \n90: ### `pyproject.toml`\n91: - Version bumped to `0.2.0`\n92: - Updated description\n93: \n94: ---\n95: \n96: ## Verification Results\n97: \n98: All tests pass:\n99: ```\n100: PASS: Final Answer parsing\n101: PASS: Action parsing\n102: PASS: Memory sliding window\n103: PASS: search_code tool\n104: PASS: Command sandboxing blocks dangerous commands\n105: PASS: git status allowed\n106: \n107: ALL TESTS PASSED\n108: ```\n109: \n110: CLI shows all 5 commands:\n111: ```\n112: Commands:\n113:   scan    Perform an automated vulnerability audit\n114:   train   Launch training for Fluxnat Coder 3B\n115:   info    Display system status\n116:   chat    Launch interactive agentic chat        ← NEW\n117:   agent   Run a one-shot agentic task            ← NEW\n118: ```\n119: \n120: ---\n121: \n122: ## How to Use\n123: \n124: ### Interactive Chat\n125: ```bash\n126: python -m smartagent.cli chat\n127: ```\n128: \n129: ### One-Shot Agent\n130: ```bash\n131: python -m smartagent.cli agent \"scan this project for SQL injection\"\n132: ```\n133: \n134: ### Classic Static Scan (unchanged)\n135: ```bash\n136: python -m smartagent.cli scan .\n137: ```\n138: \n139: > [!NOTE]\n140: > The agent requires the Fluxnat Coder 3B model (loaded in 4-bit on your GTX 1650). First run will download from `k4ran909/Fluxnat-Coder-3B` on HuggingFace (~1.8GB quantized).\n141: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
{"step_index":2163,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-16T07:45:51Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-16T13:15:51+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-10-16T13:15:52+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/k4ran/.gemini/antigravity/brain/e2c1cf9f-2dff-4bf4-a974-ef410441acfa/implementation_plan.md`\nTotal Lines: 174\nTotal Bytes: 7923\nShowing lines 1 to 174\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: # Make SmartAGENT Fully Agentic\n2: \n3: Transform SmartAGENT from a **static scanner with AI verification** into a **fully autonomous agentic security AI** that can think, plan, use tools, and act on its own.\n4: \n5: ## What Changes\n6: \n7: **Before:** You run `smartagent scan .` → static regex patterns find issues → optionally asks the LLM to verify each one.\n8: \n9: **After:** You chat with SmartAGENT like a real security engineer:\n10: ```\n11: You: scan this project for vulnerabilities\n12: Agent: [Thought] I'll start by listing all files in the project...\n13:        [Action] list_files → found 47 files\n14:        [Thought] Let me read the main app.py first...\n15:        [Action] read_file app.py → found SQL query on line 34\n16:        [Thought] This uses f-string interpolation in a SQL query — CWE-89...\n17:        [Action] scan_code → CRITICAL: SQL Injection\n18:        [Thought] Let me check if there's input sanitization upstream...\n19:        [Action] read_file utils.py → no sanitization found\n20:        [Answer] Found 3 vulnerabilities. Here's the full report...\n21: ```\n22: \n23: ---\n24: \n25: ## Architecture\n26: \n27: ```\n28: ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n29: │              Interactive CLI (Rich)           │\n30: │         smartagent chat / smartagent scan     │\n31: └──────────────────┬───────────────────────────┘\n32:                    │\n33: ┌──────────────────▼───────────────────────────┐\n34: │           ReAct Agent Loop (core.py)          │\n35: │   Thought → Action → Observation → Repeat    │\n36: │         Powered by Fluxnat Coder 3B           │\n37: └──────────┬───────────────────┬───────────────┘\n38:            │                   │\n39: ┌──────────▼────────┐ ┌───────▼──────────────┐\n40: │   Tool Registry    │ │   Conversation       │\n41: │                    │ │   Memory (memory.py)  │\n42: │  • read_file       │ │                      │\n43: │  • list_files      │ │  • Chat history      │\n44: │  • scan_code       │ │  • Sliding window    │\n45: │  • search_code     │ │  • Finding accumul.  │\n46: │  • write_report    │ └──────────────────────┘\n47: │  • web_lookup      │\n48: │  • run_command     │\n49: │  • fix_code        │\n50: └───────────────────┘\n51: ```\n52: \n53: ---\n54: \n55: ## Proposed Changes\n56: \n57: ### Agent Core — NEW modules\n58: \n59: #### [NEW] [core.py](file:///c:/Users/k4ran/OneDrive/Desktop/smartAGENT/smartagent/agent/core.py)\n60: The **ReAct reasoning loop** — the brain of the agent.\n61: - Parses LLM output for `Thought:`, `Action:`, `Action Input:`, `Final Answer:` blocks\n62: - Dispatches actions to the tool registry\n63: - Feeds `Observation:` back into the LLM for next reasoning step\n64: - Max 15 iterations per task (prevents infinite loops)\n65: - Handles tool errors gracefully\n66: \n67: #### [NEW] [tools.py](file:///c:/Users/k4ran/OneDrive/Desktop/smartAGENT/smartagent/agent/tools.py)\n68: **8 security-focused tools** the agent can call:\n69: \n70: | Tool | Description |\n71: |---|---|\n72: | `list_files` | List all files in a directory (respects ignore patterns) |\n73: | `read_file` | Read file contents with optional line range |\n74: | `search_code` | Grep/regex search across the codebase |\n75: | `scan_code` | Run static pattern scanners on a file (reuses existing scanners) |\n76: | `analyze_security` | Deep AI analysis of a code snippet (chain-of-thought) |\n77: | `write_report` | Generate a structured vulnerability report |\n78: | `web_lookup` | Look up CVE/CWE details from public databases |\n79: | `run_command` | Execute shell commands (sandboxed, with allowlist) |\n80: \n81: #### [NEW] [memory.py](file:///c:/Users/k4ran/OneDrive/Desktop/smartAGENT/smartagent/agent/memory.py)\n82: **Conversation memory** with sliding window:\n83: - Stores full chat history\n84: - Truncates to last N messages when context gets long (3B model has limited context)\n85: - Accumulates findings across multiple tool calls\n86: - Tracks which files have been scanned\n87: \n88: #### [NEW] [prompts.py](file:///c:/Users/k4ran/OneDrive/Desktop/smartAGENT/smartagent/agent/prompts.py)\n89: **ReAct system prompt** that teaches the model to use tools:\n90: - Defines the `Thought → Action → Observation` format\n91: - Lists all available tools with descriptions and input schemas\n92: - Instructs the model to reason step-by-step before acting\n93: - Includes the Fluxnat Coder 3B identity and security expertise\n94: \n95: #### [NEW] [\\_\\_init\\_\\_.py](file:///c:/Users/k4ran/OneDrive/Desktop/smartAGENT/smartagent/agent/__init__.py)\n96: Package init exposing `SmartAgent` class.\n97: \n98: ---\n99: \n100: ### CLI Updates\n101: \n102: #### [MODIFY] [cli.py](file:///c:/Users/k4ran/OneDrive/Desktop/smartAGENT/smartagent/cli.py)\n103: Add a new **`chat`** command for interactive agentic mode:\n104: - `smartagent chat` — opens an interactive terminal session where you talk to the agent\n105: - `smartagent agent \"scan this project for vulns\"` — one-shot agentic task\n106: - Existing `scan` and `train` commands stay untouched\n107: \n108: ---\n109: \n110: ### Model Updates\n111: \n112: #### [MODIFY] [model.py](file:///c:/Users/k4ran/OneDrive/Desktop/smartAGENT/smartagent/ai/model.py)\n113: - Fix the `Tuple[Any, Any]` type hint (missing import)\n114: - Add a `generate_stream()` method for real-time token streaming in chat mode\n115: - Add `max_context_length` property so memory can calculate truncation\n116: \n117: ---\n118: \n119: ### Config Updates\n120: \n121: #### [MODIFY] [config.py](file:///c:/Users/k4ran/OneDrive/Desktop/smartAGENT/smartagent/config.py)\n122: Add agent-specific config fields:\n123: - `max_agent_iterations: int = 15` — loop safety limit\n124: - `agent_temperature: float = 0.3` — slightly higher for reasoning diversity\n125: - `memory_window: int = 20` — max messages to keep in context\n126: - `allowed_commands: list` — sandboxed shell command allowlist\n127: \n128: ---\n129: \n130: ### Dependencies\n131: \n132: #### [MODIFY] [pyproject.toml](file:///c:/Users/k4ran/OneDrive/Desktop/smartAGENT/pyproject.toml)\n133: - Add `prompt_toolkit>=3.0.0` for interactive chat input with history\n134: - Add `readchar>=4.0.0` for key handling\n135: - No other new dependencies — everything else uses existing packages (rich, transformers, torch)\n136: \n137: ---\n138: \n139: ## File Summary\n140: \n141: | File | Action | Purpose |\n142: |---|---|---|\n143: | `smartagent/agent/__init__.py` | **NEW** | Package init |\n144: | `smartagent/agent/core.py` | **NEW** | ReAct agent loop |\n145: | `smartagent/agent/tools.py` | **NEW** | 8 security tools |\n146: | `smartagent/agent/memory.py` | **NEW** | Conversation memory |\n147: | `smartagent/agent/prompts.py` | **NEW** | ReAct system prompt |\n148: | `smartagent/cli.py` | MODIFY | Add `chat` + `agent` commands |\n149: | `smartagent/ai/model.py` | MODIFY | Fix type hint, add streaming |\n150: | `smartagent/config.py` | MODIFY | Add agent config fields |\n151: | `pyproject.toml` | MODIFY | Add prompt_toolkit dep |\n152: \n153: > [!IMPORTANT]\n154: > **VRAM Constraint:** Your GTX 1650 has 4GB VRAM. The model loads in 4-bit quantization (~1.8GB), leaving ~2GB for context. The ReAct loop keeps reasoning chains short (max 15 iterations) and memory uses a sliding window to prevent OOM.\n155: \n156: > [!NOTE]\n157: > **No Ollama.** Everything runs via `transformers` + `bitsandbytes` directly. The existing `ModelManager` singleton is reused — no new inference backend.\n158: \n159: ## Verification Plan\n160: \n161: ### Automated Tests\n162: ```bash\n163: # Test agent tools in isolation\n164: python -m pytest tests/test_agent_tools.py -v\n165: \n166: # Test ReAct loop with mock LLM\n167: python -m pytest tests/test_agent_core.py -v\n168: ```\n169: \n170: ### Manual Verification\n171: 1. `smartagent chat` — interactive session, ask \"who are you?\" → should identify as Fluxnat Coder 3B\n172: 2. `smartagent agent \"scan this project\"` — should autonomously discover files, scan them, and produce a report\n173: 3. `smartagent scan .` — existing static scan still works unchanged\n174: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
